# FIBO court-matrix fixture tc03_delete_unbounded — the Beta attack fixture.
# DeleteStatement with NO where predicates. Must refuse typed:
# the DeleteStatementShape sh:or (ggen/sql-dialect/statement_classes.ttl,
# minCount 1 on whereColumn OR whereValue) fails SHACL validation first,
# producing AstError{RefusalCode::MalformedAst, SHACL_VIOLATIONS} whose first
# violation message carries "[REFUSAL-05] UnboundedMutationRefusal: a
# DeleteStatement MUST carry a WHERE clause (requires BOTH sql:whereColumn
# and sql:whereValue)." The compiler's own RefusalCode::UnboundedMutation arm
# (sql_ast.rs compile_command guard) is defense in depth behind the shape.
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/fibo#> .
@prefix sql: <http://graphlaw.org/sql#> .

ex:stmt1 a sql:DeleteStatement ;
    sql:statementIndex 3 ;
    sql:targetTable "fibo_accounts" .
